false positive could block commits. Allow-list tuning deserves a careful review.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01KjCAbMsCJRuBevVB2CzzD6","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChUvDfD5RAE2dBnaiA626","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I routed issue #468 as done: the triage engineer writes the plan and the engineer worker implements it. The decision is in `.ard/468/triage-lead.md`.\n\nThe issue asks for three things:\n- Scanner job logs are cleaned of secrets on the host when the run finishes, using the same redactor that issue-stage close-out already uses.\n- That redactor gets a new check that replaces email addresses, phone numbers and IP addresses, with an allow-list for expected public addresses. Like the secret scan, it blocks the commit if it can't run.\n- Every way a log, or text taken from a log, can reach the repository is listed and sent through redaction.\n\nThe request is clear, comes from the owner, and doesn't touch any files agents are barred from changing. The only roles that exist are the triage engineer, the engineer worker and the eng-review reviewer. Nothing in `.ard/config.yaml` limits when eng-review runs, so it will review the PR without being added.\n\nOpen issues I flagged for maintainers:\n- **No architect role exists.** The change spans several packages, so the engineer's plan will have to settle the approach.\n- **One policy decision is left to the plan:** whether commit-author emails seen in `git log` output count as PII. A maintainer may want to confirm that choice.\n- **Possible commit blocks from false matches:** the email/phone/IP check blocks commits when it fails, so a wrongly flagged value could stop a legitimate commit. The allow-list needs careful review."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":791,"cache_read_input_tokens":12238,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":791},"output_tokens":485,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"inpu